# npm config — enforces the dependency-pinning posture (S01.11).
#
# Why this file exists: the Privacy Baseline's dep-tree gates (S01.7
# `check:deps`, S01.10 `check:telemetry`) read `node_modules/` and
# assert the dep tree is clean. Those assertions are only meaningful
# if `node_modules/` is reproducible across machines. Reproducibility
# starts at install time: this file is the contributor-side sibling
# to CI's `npm ci` (S01.5 ci.yml:41).
#
# `save-exact=true`: when a contributor runs
#   npm install <pkg> --save-dev
# the dep is recorded as an exact version (`"5.1.1"`) instead of
# `^5.1.1`. Defends against the drift AC1 is meant to catch on the
# CI side. Per S01.11 AC4.
#
# `package-lock=true`: ensures the lockfile is created/updated on
# install. Defends against an accidental `npm config set
# package-lock false` on a contributor's machine silently suppressing
# the lockfile.
#
# `engine-strict=true`: enforces the `engines.node` field in
# `package.json` (currently `>=20.0.0`). A contributor running an
# older Node version will see a clear error at install time rather
# than mysterious test failures later.
#
# This file is structural, not aspirational. It is tested by
# `tests/dependency-pinning.test.ts` (S01.11 AC4).

save-exact=true
package-lock=true
engine-strict=true
